      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Economic Overview"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Haryana is a major contributor to India's central pool of food grains, earning it a reputation as a primary agricultural powerhouse.",
        "Gurugram and Faridabad serve as the main engines of industrial and service sector growth, particularly in automotive manufacturing, IT, and ITeS.",
        "Prominent national research institutions such as the National Dairy Research Institute (NDRI) in Karnal and Central Institute for Research on Buffaloes (CIRB) in Hisar are situated in Haryana.",
        "The state features extensive canal irrigation networks, with the Western Yamuna Canal playing a vital role in agricultural productivity."
      ],
      "id": "42n3gax"
    },
